/-!
# Flatness of a sheaf of modules is local on the site

Let `(C, O)` be a ringed site and let `M` be a sheaf of `O`-modules. If `V : ι → C` is a family
of objects covering the final object and the restriction `M|_{V i}` of `M` to the localization of
the site at `V i` is a flat `O|_{V i}`-module for every `i`, then `M` is a flat `O`-module.

This is the descent direction of the locality of flatness. It is what promotes a *slicewise*
flatness statement — such as the flatness of the lowest cokernel of a bounded above flat complex
of Tor amplitude in `[a, b]`,
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.DerivedTensorProduct.isFlat_cokernel_of_hasTorAmplitude`, which is
available over each member of a covering supplied by locally finite Tor dimension — to a
statement about the covered object.

## Main results

* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.mono_of_mono_over`: **monomorphy of a morphism of sheaves of modules is
  local on the site.** A morphism whose restriction to each member of a family of objects
  covering the final object is a monomorphism is a monomorphism.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isFlat_of_iso_freeUniverse`: flatness is invariant under isomorphism,
  which is what lets a slicewise statement about the cokernel of a restricted differential be
  read as a statement about the restriction of a cokernel. The existing
  `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isFlat_of_iso` is the same statement pinned to a ringed site whose three
  universes agree.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isFlat_of_coversTop`: **flatness of a sheaf of modules is local on the
  site.**
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isFlat_of_ofArrows_of_isTerminal`: the same with the covering given as a
  covering sieve generated by a family of arrows into a terminal object, which is the shape a
  covering of the whole site is produced in.

## Route

Flatness asserts the exactness of tensoring with `M`, so it is not a property of a single
morphism and its locality is not formal. It reduces to one, however: tensoring with a sheaf of
modules is always right exact (Tag 05NB,
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.preservesFiniteColimits_sheafTensorFlipObj`), and a right exact additive
functor between abelian categories is exact as soon as it preserves monomorphisms
(`Stacks.Sites.AbelianLowerShriek.exactFunctor_of_preservesMonomorphisms`). So the content is the
locality of monomorphy, together with the comparison
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.sheafTensorOverIso` of the restriction of a tensor product with the
tensor product of the restrictions, and the naturality of that comparison in the variable being
tensored, `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.sheafTensorOverIso_naturality_left`.

Monomorphy is local because its obstruction is an object rather than a morphism: in an abelian
category `f` is a monomorphism exactly when `ker f` is zero
(`CategoryTheory.Preadditive.mono_iff_isZero_kernel`), restriction to a slice preserves finite
limits and therefore kernels
(`Stacks.SheafOfModules.LocalCokernel.overFunctor_preservesFiniteLimits`, which needs no
hypothesis on the site), and a sheaf of modules all of whose restrictions to the members of a
covering family vanish vanishes — applied to the zero endomorphism of `ker f`, this is the
locality of invertibility, `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QcohRestrictEquiv.isIso_of_isIso_over`.

## Implementation notes

The three universes of the ringed site — objects, morphisms, sections of the structure sheaf —
are independent, and the index type of the covering family has a fourth independent universe.
That is what makes the result usable on the constant-coefficient ringed site of Tag 03TR, whose
three universes are `u + 1`, `u` and `max (u + 1) w r`; a statement pinned to the diagonal would
not be.

Two spellings of the sheaf of rings on a slice are in play:
`(Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O).over V`, which restriction of modules produces, and
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (X.O.over V)`, which the tensor product on the slice is
indexed by. They are the same term — `(Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (X.O.over V))` is
both — but only after unfolding definitions that instance search does not unfold, so a `Mono`
hypothesis stated at one spelling is not found by instance search at the other. Every step that
would otherwise be left to instance search is therefore applied as an explicit term, where the
ambient definitional equality is available; `mono_of_mono_sq` exists for exactly that reason, the
instance `CategoryTheory.mono_comp` being unusable here.

## What is not done

**The converse is not proved**: that the restriction of a flat sheaf of modules to a slice is
flat. Tensoring with `M|_V` has to be shown exact on sheaves of `O|_V`-modules, and a
monomorphism of those does not come from the whole site, so the argument needs the extension by
zero `j_!` of sheaves of modules, left adjoint to restriction, together with its exactness and
the identification `j^* j_! ≅ id`. None of the three is available in the tree for sheaves of
modules on a general site. Consequently the statements here are implications and not
equivalences.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 03ER](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03ER)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 05NB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05NB)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03TT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03TT)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 04IX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04IX)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry

universe u v w

namespace Stacks.SheafOfModules

/-- Monomorphy across a commuting square whose two vertical maps are isomorphisms. This is
`CategoryTheory.mono_of_mono_fac` with the monomorphy of the composite `eA.hom ≫ m` supplied as a
term rather than by instance search, which cannot see it when the two sides of the square live in
two spellings of one category. -/
private theorem mono_of_mono_sq {D : Type*} [Category* D] {A B A' B' : D}
    (f : A ⟶ B) {eA : A ≅ A'} {eB : B ≅ B'} {m : A' ⟶ B'}
    (h : f ≫ eB.hom = eA.hom ≫ m) (hm : Mono m) : Mono f :=
  have := hm
  mono_of_mono_fac h

section MonoLocality

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{w}}
  [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{w}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
  [∀ U : C, HasSheafify (J.over U) AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
  [∀ U : C, (J.over U).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]

omit [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{w}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}] in
/-- **Monomorphy of a morphism of sheaves of modules is local on the site.** If `V : ι → C` is a
family of objects covering the final object and the restriction of `φ` to the localization of the
site at `V i` is a monomorphism for every `i`, then `φ` is a monomorphism.

The kernel of `φ` restricts to the kernel of the restriction of `φ`, restriction preserving
finite limits, so each of its restrictions vanishes; a sheaf of modules whose restrictions to the
members of a covering family all vanish vanishes, by the locality of invertibility applied to its
zero endomorphism. -/
theorem mono_of_mono_over {ι : Type*} {V : ι → C} (hV : J.CoversTop V)
    {M N : _root_.SheafOfModules.{w} R} (φ : M ⟶ N)
    (h : ∀ i, Mono (φ.over (V i))) : Mono φ := by
  rw [Preadditive.mono_iff_isZero_kernel]
  have hover : ∀ i, IsZero ((kernel φ).over (V i)) := by
    intro i
    have := h i
    have : PreservesFiniteLimits (_root_.SheafOfModules.overFunctor R (V i)) :=
      LocalCokernel.overFunctor_preservesFiniteLimits (V i)
    exact IsZero.of_iso (IsZero.of_iso (isZero_zero _) (kernel.ofMono (φ.over (V i))))
      (PreservesKernel.iso (_root_.SheafOfModules.overFunctor R (V i)) φ)
  have hiso : IsIso (0 : kernel φ ⟶ kernel φ) := by
    refine Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QcohRestrictEquiv.isIso_of_isIso_over hV _ fun i => ?_
    have hz : (0 : kernel φ ⟶ kernel φ).over (V i) = 0 := Functor.map_zero _ _ _
    rw [hz, (hover i).eq_of_src 0 (𝟙 _)]
    infer_instance
  rw [IsZero.iff_id_eq_zero]
  exact (IsIso.hom_inv_id (0 : kernel φ ⟶ kernel φ)).symm.trans zero_comp

end MonoLocality

section Flat

-- The sections universe `w` is free, so Mathlib's size-restricted instances do not supply the
-- sheaf-condition composition that `AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFlat` is stated through.
attribute [local instance] Stacks.hasSheafCompose_forget₂_commRingCat

variable {X : RingedSite.{u, v, w}}
  [HasSheafify X.J AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
  [X.J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
  [∀ U : X.C, HasSheafify (X.J.over U) AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
  [∀ U : X.C, (X.J.over U).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]

/-- Sheafification on a slice, at the spelling of the localized ringed site. -/
local instance sliceHasSheafify (U : X.C) : HasSheafify (X.over U).J AddCommGrpCat.{w} :=
  (inferInstance : ∀ U : X.C, HasSheafify (X.J.over U) AddCommGrpCat.{w}) U

/-- Local bijectivity of the weak equivalences on a slice, at the localized spelling. -/
local instance sliceWEqualsLocallyBijective (U : X.C) :
    (X.over U).J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w} :=
  (inferInstance : ∀ U : X.C, (X.J.over U).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}) U

omit [∀ U : X.C, HasSheafify (X.J.over U) AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
  [∀ U : X.C, (X.J.over U).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}] in
/-- **Flatness is invariant under isomorphism of sheaves of modules**, with the three universes of
the ringed site independent. Tensoring with isomorphic sheaves of modules gives isomorphic
functors, and exactness of a functor is invariant under isomorphism.

`Stacks.SheafOfModules.isFlat_of_iso` is the same statement on a ringed site whose three
universes agree, which is where its consumers in
`StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Cohomology.KFlat.ResolutionExists` live; that pin is what makes
a second statement necessary here rather than a reuse. The transport is made along
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor`, whose exactness flatness is read off by
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.exactFunctor_sheafTensorFlip_of_isFlat`, and not along
`AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.sheafTensorRight` directly. -/
theorem isFlat_of_iso_freeUniverse {M N : RingedSite.Modules.{u, v, w} X} (e : M ≅ N)
    (h : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFlat.{v, u, w, w} (O := X.O) M) :
    AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFlat.{v, u, w, w} (O := X.O) N :=
  isFlat_of_exactFunctor_sheafTensorFlip X.O N
    ((exactFunctor _ _).prop_of_iso
      ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, v, w, w, w} X.O).flip.mapIso e)
      (exactFunctor_sheafTensorFlip_of_isFlat X.O M h))

/-- **Flatness of a sheaf of modules is local on the site.** If `V : ι → C` is a family of objects
covering the final object of the site and the restriction of `M` to the localization of the ringed
site at `V i` is flat for every `i`, then `M` is flat.

Tensoring with `M` is right exact in any case, so the content is that it preserves
monomorphisms. A monomorphism tensored with `M` restricts, by the comparison
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.sheafTensorOverIso` and its naturality, to the restricted
monomorphism tensored with the restriction of `M`, which is a monomorphism by the hypothesis; and
monomorphy is local. -/
theorem isFlat_of_coversTop {ι : Type*} {V : ι → X.C} (hV : X.J.CoversTop V)
    (M : RingedSite.Modules.{u, v, w} X)
    (hM : ∀ i, AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFlat.{v, max u v, w, w}
      (O := (X.over (V i)).O) (M.over (V i))) :
    AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFlat.{v, u, w, w} (O := X.O) M := by
  refine isFlat_of_exactFunctor_sheafTensorFlip X.O M ?_
  let T := Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, v, w, w, w} X.O
  have : PreservesFiniteColimits (T.flip.obj M) :=
    preservesFiniteColimits_sheafTensorFlipObj X.O M
  have : (T.flip.obj M).Additive :=
    have := preservesBinaryBiproducts_of_preservesBinaryCoproducts (T.flip.obj M)
    Functor.additive_of_preservesBinaryBiproducts _
  have : (T.flip.obj M).PreservesMonomorphisms := by
    refine ⟨fun {A B} g hg => ?_⟩
    have : Mono g := hg
    refine mono_of_mono_over hV _ fun i => ?_
    change Mono ((((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, v, w, w, w} X.O).map g).app M).over
      (V i))
    have hmg : Mono (g.over (V i)) :=
      have := preservesHomology_overFunctor
        (R := (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) (V i)
      inferInstance
    have hslice : Mono ((((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{max u v, v, w, w, w}
        (X.O.over (V i))).map (g.over (V i)))).app (M.over (V i))) := by
      have hF := exactFunctor_sheafTensorFlip_of_isFlat (X.O.over (V i)) (M.over (V i)) (hM i)
      rw [exactFunctor_iff] at hF
      obtain ⟨hlim, hcolim⟩ := hF
      have : ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{max u v, v, w, w, w}
          (X.O.over (V i))).flip.obj (M.over (V i))).Additive :=
        Functor.additive_of_preserves_binary_products _
      exact @Functor.map_mono _ _ _ _ ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{max u v,
        v, w, w, w} (X.O.over (V i))).flip.obj (M.over (V i))) inferInstance _ _
        (g.over (V i)) hmg
    exact mono_of_mono_sq _ (RingedSite.sheafTensorOverIso_naturality_left X (V i) g M) hslice
  exact Stacks.Sites.AbelianLowerShriek.exactFunctor_of_preservesMonomorphisms _

/-- **Flatness of a sheaf of modules descends along a covering of a terminal object.** If the
sieve generated by a family of arrows `V i ⟶ U` into a terminal object `U` of the site is
covering, and the restriction of `M` to the localization at each `V i` is flat, then `M` is flat.

This is the shape a covering of the whole site is produced in, for instance by
`exists_finite_covering_hasTorAmplitude_of_locallyHasFiniteTorDimension` at a quasi-compact
object: a sieve on an object, generated by finitely many arrows. Over a terminal object the sieve
generated by the arrows is the sieve generated by their sources, so the family covers the final
object. -/
@[sga "6 I 5.5" "First assertion of 5.5"]
theorem isFlat_of_ofArrows_of_isTerminal {U : X.C} (hU : IsTerminal U)
    {ι : Type*} {V : ι → X.C} (f : ∀ i, V i ⟶ U) (hcov : Sieve.ofArrows V f ∈ X.J U)
    (M : RingedSite.Modules.{u, v, w} X)
    (hM : ∀ i, AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFlat.{v, max u v, w, w}
      (O := (X.over (V i)).O) (M.over (V i))) :
    AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFlat.{v, u, w, w} (O := X.O) M :=
  isFlat_of_coversTop
    ((X.J.coversTop_iff_of_isTerminal U hU V).2
      ((Sieve.ofArrows_eq_ofObjects hU V f) ▸ hcov)) M hM

end Flat

end Stacks.SheafOfModules

end
